;. /cited_assertions_flow
  ;@ /flow/definition cited_assertions
  ;= Propose and review source-qualified assertions

    Subject identity is supplied explicitly. A provider proposes interpretations;
    deterministic validation checks their shape and exact quoted source bytes.
    This establishes citation fidelity, not the truth of an interpretation.
    The provider's acceptance decision and reason remain on each assertion.
    Rejected proposals and original captures remain in the execution trace.

    ;@ /flow/input sources
    ;= Captured structured source evidence

    ;@ /flow/input subject
    ;= Explicit subject and question
      Bind an own record containing subject as a native reference or explicit
      path, and question as text. A Semidoc heading with a subject path attribute
      can supply its title as the question. Shared names do not merge identities.

    ;@ /flow/input projection
    ;= Selected native projection
      Bind the raw x record of the published Grove graph report, normally
      /0x11/gov/graph/report. It contains the compiled spun constructor. Select
      a retained version or a frozen selection cell to pin the policy. A live
      binding deliberately follows publication; attempts retain their capture.
      The optional graph mount supplies this policy; the shared flow harness
      does not depend on graph or install its own copy of that policy.

    ;@ /flow/step proposed ;/0x11/gov/flows/operations/cartography/propose
    ;@ /flow/bind sources sources
    ;@ /flow/bind subject subject
    ;= Request bounded cited assertions through the shared provider
      The captured validator refuses missing quotations, invented source text,
      invalid fields and malformed judgments before the request can complete.
      Rejected responses keep their existing native hole and retry operation.

    ;@ /flow/step claims ;/0x11/gov/flows/operations/cartography/collect
    ;@ /flow/bind responses proposed
    ;= Expose validated assertions as native records

    ;@ /flow/step projected ;/0x11/gov/flows/operations/cartography/project
    ;@ /flow/bind claims claims
    ;@ /flow/bind projection projection
    ;= Apply the selected ordinary Grove constructor
      The projection may select and annotate assertions. It may not change
      their subject, value, citation, acceptance judgment or other qualifiers.

    ;@ /flow/step judged ;/0x11/gov/flows/operations/cartography/judge
    ;@ /flow/bind claims projected
    ;= Retain a judgment on the selected evidence
      Empty evidence or a marked conflict leaves this demand unresolved even
      if the provider claims completion. Changed bound evidence creates a new
      attempt through the same native lifecycle. Unchanged failures require
      an explicit retry. No private scheduler or automatic retry loop exists.

    ;@ /flow/step reviewed ;/0x11/gov/flows/operations/cartography/reviewed_sources
    ;@ /flow/bind responses judged
    ;@ /flow/bind sources sources
    ;= Retain reviewed assertions alongside the original source envelopes

    ;@ /flow/result reviewed
    ;= Evidence ready for a document procedure
